    <div class="case-study-body">
      <h4>Sketches and wireframes</h4>
      <p><strong>Early sketches</strong> &mdash; Sketches helped the team decide what was required in the initial stages of development.</p>
      <p><strong>On-boarding concept</strong> &mdash; Website on-boarding sketches.</p>
      <p><strong>Axure prototype</strong> &mdash; An Axure prototype was developed to understand user interactions and enable testing.</p>

      <h4>User testing</h4>
      <p>Testing the initial sign up experience, including form submission and online statement upload. One-hour sessions were conducted and captured. Key findings were documented and presented back to the team.</p>

      <h4>Participant surveys</h4>
      <p><strong>Survey one</strong> &mdash; Background research.</p>
      <p><strong>Survey two</strong> &mdash; Product first impressions.</p>

      <h4>Brand identity and style guide</h4>
      <p><em>Details to come.</em></p>

      <h4>Hi-fidelity design</h4>
      <p>Hi-fidelity designs were created based off Sketch wireframes and sent to the team for approval.</p>

      <h4>Specification sheet</h4>
      <p>Once designs were approved, a spec sheet was supplied to the developers.</p>

      <h4>Responsive design</h4>
      <p>It was important everyone in the team understood how the design was going to translate to tablet and mobile.</p>

      <h4>Customer presentation pack</h4>
      <p>Data overview, super story, investment breakdown.</p>
    </div>

